<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8"?>
<!--
  SmartAssist accessibility service config (File No 89) — round no60.

  Traced against SmartAssistAccessibilityEngine.kt (HEAD 850341fe):

  NO60-D5 (PROVEN): flagRetrieveInteractiveWindows REMOVED. The flag
  only matters if the service calls getWindows(); the service never does
  (zero getWindows()/windows references in the service). It only reads
  rootInActiveWindow (onServiceConnected seed + F34), which needs
  canRetrieveWindowContent="true" — kept. Removing an unused flag
  changes no behaviour; keeping it overstated what the service does.

  VERIFIED, not defects: the three declared event types are exactly the
  three the service handles — typeWindowStateChanged (foreground-package
  trust gate), typeTouchInteractionStart/End (UserTouchState) — no
  declared type is unhandled and no handled type is undeclared.
  canPerformGestures="true" is USED (dispatchGesture in the gesture
  path). notificationTimeout="0" is deliberate (touch latency).
  canRetrieveWindowContent="true" is USED (rootInActiveWindow seed).

  NO60-D6 (PROVEN, documented not changed): feedbackHaptic is declared
  but the service emits NO haptic feedback — no Vibrator/vibrate call
  anywhere in the service. The attribute is inert as declared. It is
  KEPT deliberately: removing it would let the system fall back to its
  default feedback type for this service, which is a behaviour change
  for accessibility users that cannot be verified in the sandbox. If
  Ed wants it gone, that is his call (queued).

  TOUCH-FALLBACK (2026-11-25): flagSendMotionEvents declared — the v268
  session PROVED the touch-interaction path starved (A11Y_FLOW
  touchEventAgeMs=-1 all session) while other events arrived, so this
  ROM withholds TYPE_TOUCH_INTERACTION_* despite a correct mask. The flag
  (API 36, value 0x4000, attrs.xml-verified) makes the system also
  deliver raw MotionEvents to the service's onMotionEvent — a second,
  independent touch signal. The service code re-asserts the same flag
  on every bind (onServiceConnected) and in the watchdog heal, so the
  declaration and the effective info cannot drift apart. FLAG_REQUEST_
  TOUCH_EXPLORATION_MODE is deliberately NOT declared (explore-by-touch
  would break gameplay input).
-->
<accessibility-service xmlns:android="http://schemas.android.com/apk/res/android"
    android:description="@string/accessibility_service_description"
    android:accessibilityEventTypes="typeWindowStateChanged|typeTouchInteractionStart|typeTouchInteractionEnd"
    android:accessibilityFeedbackType="feedbackHaptic"
    android:accessibilityFlags="flagSendMotionEvents"
    android:notificationTimeout="0"
    android:canRetrieveWindowContent="true"
    android:canPerformGestures="true" />
